WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:16.680
Two hundred and fifty thousand people are in Washington for the inauguration, but for

00:16.680 --> 00:23.440
those unable to get there, the universal newspaper newsreel is rushing pictures of the epic ceremony

00:23.440 --> 00:27.200
by the fastest air express plane in the country.

00:27.200 --> 00:32.240
The speedy plane takes off and soars over the national capital, even while President

00:32.240 --> 00:35.800
Roosevelt is still on the inaugural stand.

00:35.800 --> 00:41.120
At two hundred and thirty miles an hour, the record-breaking air express twists its historic

00:41.120 --> 00:46.160
freight to the screen, arriving at New York while newspaper wires are still hot with the

00:46.160 --> 00:50.920
story of the great event, and while the radio still roars with acclamations for the new

00:50.920 --> 00:52.640
president.

00:52.640 --> 00:57.960
At the airport, a fast car with police escort is waiting, and the film is transferred almost

00:57.960 --> 01:00.720
as soon as the plane touches the ground.

01:00.720 --> 01:05.540
No bet is overlooked in the race against time to serve the newsreel public, and the universal

01:05.540 --> 01:09.240
newspaper newsreel is establishing a record for speed.

01:09.240 --> 01:13.320
Here they come, on the last lap.

01:13.320 --> 01:17.480
And here it is, the beginning of the greatest drama in American affairs, the creation of

01:17.480 --> 01:19.600
a new chief executive.

01:19.600 --> 01:24.000
According to time-honored custom, the retiring president and the president-elect ride together

01:24.000 --> 01:28.480
from the White House with congressional escort down the long and crowd-packed Pennsylvania

01:28.480 --> 01:32.160
Avenue to the capital, where Roosevelt is to take the oath of office.

01:32.160 --> 01:34.600
Enthusiasm is at its height.

01:34.600 --> 01:38.960
Never was there such a joyful, jubilant, yelling, applauding inauguration crowd.

01:38.960 --> 01:42.520
Roosevelt is the nation's idol here today.

01:42.520 --> 01:46.920
Thousands of Americans are here to cheer the birth of a new era in national affairs, a

01:46.920 --> 01:51.000
New Deal era, which is supposed to pull the country out of its chaos.

01:51.000 --> 01:58.800
The hosts of democracy are here to celebrate the greatest party victory of all time.

01:58.800 --> 02:01.920
And now, everything is ready for the big moment.

02:01.920 --> 02:06.280
Chief Justice Hughes of the United States Supreme Court prepares to administer the oath

02:06.280 --> 02:11.120
of office to Franklin D. Roosevelt, making him the 62nd president...

02:11.120 --> 02:22.640
You, Franklin Delano Roosevelt, you solemnly swear that you will faithfully execute the

02:22.640 --> 02:31.200
office of President of the United States, and will, to the best of your ability, preserve,

02:31.200 --> 02:39.560
protect and defend the Constitution of the United States, so help you God.

02:39.560 --> 02:46.760
I, Franklin Delano Roosevelt, do solemnly swear that I will faithfully execute the office

02:46.760 --> 02:53.600
of President of the United States, and will, to the best of my ability, preserve, protect

02:53.600 --> 02:59.560
and defend the Constitution of the United States, so help me God.

02:59.560 --> 03:13.040
This is a day of national consecration, and I am certain that on this day, my fellow Americans

03:13.040 --> 03:23.240
expect that on my induction into the presidency, I will address them with a candor and a decision

03:23.240 --> 03:26.960
which the present situation of our people impels.

03:26.960 --> 03:33.640
I am prepared, under my constitutional duty, to recommend the measures that a stricken

03:33.640 --> 03:38.280
nation in the midst of a stricken world may require.

03:38.280 --> 03:47.320
These measures, or such other measures, as the Congress may build out of its experience

03:47.320 --> 03:54.800
and wisdom, I shall seek within my constitutional authority to bring to speedy adoption.

03:54.800 --> 04:01.320
But in the event that the Congress shall fail to take one of these two forces, in the event

04:01.320 --> 04:08.160
that the national emergency is still critical, I shall not evade the clear course of duty

04:08.160 --> 04:10.560
that will then confront me.

04:10.560 --> 04:18.840
I shall ask the Congress for the one remaining instrument to meet the crisis, broad executive

04:18.840 --> 04:26.840
power, to wage a war against the emergency as great as the power that would be given

04:26.840 --> 04:34.280
to me if we were in fact invaded by a foreign foe.

04:34.280 --> 04:42.880
This nation is asking for action and action now.

04:42.880 --> 04:52.120
In this dedication of a nation, we humbly ask the blessing of God.

04:52.120 --> 04:57.920
May he protect each and every one of us.

04:57.920 --> 05:13.480
May he guide me in the days to come.

05:13.480 --> 05:36.040
May he protect each and every one of us.

05:36.040 --> 06:03.560
May he guide me in the days to come.

06:03.560 --> 06:32.080
May he guide me in the days to come.

06:32.080 --> 07:00.600
May he guide me in the days to come.

07:00.600 --> 07:29.120
May he guide me in the days to come.

07:29.120 --> 07:35.120
More power to you, President Roosevelt.

07:35.120 --> 08:01.760
The entire country's behind you, thrilled with hope and patriotism.

